// Velati journal for the Long Watch (session 73). Written when the chapter ends, on a copy of the state. No choices.
@chapter lw_journal_2000s
@title Velati Journal: The Last Ordinary Year
@book unchained
@version 1

# start
## Entry in the great book
> Entered in the winter, by the reader of the third table, to be read by no one under the rank of keeper.
There has been a great failing of banks in the western world. One house of long standing has come through it.
?if lw.bailout == "lent"
  It lent, openly, and took a bank for its pains. The street is afraid of it and has begun to say so in print.
?elif lw.bailout == "stood"
  It stood quietly behind a friend, and nobody was told. The friend is still open. The friend does not know whom to thank.
?else
  It let a friend fall, and bought the pieces. It is a thing that the Order has watched for two thousand years, and never learned to like.
?end
?if lw.fall == "took"
  A rival house has been taken in. I did not think that I would live to write that sentence.
?elif lw.fall == "bought"
  A rival house has been bought, and scattered. It was done without malice. That is the worst of it.
?else
  A rival house has been let fall. Someone was watching, and did nothing, and I have written down who.
?end
The old man in Geneva has telephoned. I do not know what was said. I know that the whole Order has been awake since.
=> endbook
